<title>USA: Pacific Enterprises/Enova deal seen saving $1.2bln.</title>
<headline>Pacific Enterprises/Enova deal seen saving $1.2bln.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proposed merger between Pacific Enterprises, and Enova Corp will generate cost savings of $1.2 billion over 10 years, executives of both firms said during a conference call with reporters.</p>
<p>The estimate is before tax, but net of an estimated $240 million, which will need to be spent to achieve the savings, they said.</p>
</text>
